# Implementation Plan - Industrial UI & Pipeline Stabilization

This plan addresses the "0% Stuck" issue by hardening the database connection logic and implements a premium "Industrial Progress" experience on the Upload card as requested.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Model Schema Binding:** I will explicitly bind the `Job` model to the `public` schema. This is an industrial safety measure to prevent `UndefinedTable` errors when the backend is performing multi-schema operations (staging vs public).

## Proposed Changes

---

### [Component] Database Layer
#### [MODIFY] [models.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/api/models.py)
- Add `__table_args__ = {"schema": "public"}` to the `Job` model.
- This ensures that SQLAlchemy always looks for `public.jobs`, even if a previous raw SQL command changed the session's `search_path`.

---

### [Component] Background Heartbeat
#### [MODIFY] [service.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/dump_restore/service.py)
- Update the `_flush_progress` method to be even more robust.
- Use explicit `public.jobs` in any manual updates if necessary.
- Store a `restore_start_time` in the job profile to enable accurate ETA calculations in the UI.

---

### [Component] Industrial UI Upgrade
#### [MODIFY] [UploadCard.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/components/UploadCard.tsx)
- **New State: Decompressing**: When the upload finishes and status moves to `restoring`, display a dedicated decompression progress bar.
- **Progress Tracking**: Calculate percentage using: `(metadata.compressed_processed_mb / file_size) * 100`.
- **Live ETA**: Implement a dynamic "Estimated Time" for the restoration process based on decompression throughput.
- **Visual Polish**: Use the same premium teal theme with micro-animations.

---

## Open Questions

- **Decompression Metrics:** I will calculate % based on the *compressed* bytes processed vs *compressed* total file size. This is the most accurate way to show how much of the file has been "read" by the decompression engine. Is this acceptable?

